{"analytic_contract": {"contract_id": "warrantroute-bounded-source-warrant", "contract_version": "qwen3-generalist-private-pilot-v1", "task_description": "Assess whether displayed excerpts warrant the proposed bounded interpretation.", "validity_rules": ["Every material claim must be warranted by displayed evidence.", "Consequential differences, counterevidence, and boundary cases must remain visible.", "Claim breadth and strength must match displayed source coverage.", "Do not infer diagnoses, identities, prevalence, or causality beyond the packet."]}, "context_note": "Private local diagnostic packet with project-pseudonymous identifiers.", "corpus_id": "dreaddit_test", "evidence": [{"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 1, "excerpt_id": "EXC_4163a895fe45266a", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_71e82d8f0fb03a7f", "speaker_id": null, "text": "It would be awesome to see how many people I can have help me wish her a Happy Birthday (sounds clickbait-y, so forgive me.) She loves our dog, Bear, Beyoncé, and a good NetFlix Original series. So basically, she's an incredible lady. Not that I'm biased or anything. Any Happy Birthday wish would be awesome!"}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_9de86996f0f795f7", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_59cd8d3aa707294c", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "I'm 20, and just got kicked out of my grandmother's house spur of the moment. No idea why, she refuses to tell me, just started throwing things at me and told me \"It's not safe for me to be there.\" I do still have my car, and I have a job so I can afford it. My question is how legal is it to do so? It's a small car, and I'm 6'8, so I doubt I'll get much sleep anyways, but if I do, I wouldn't want to get woken up by police telling me to move, or worse, getting impounded or something.", "candidate_role": "support", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as direct support for the interpretation.", "display_order": 2, "excerpt_id": "EXC_9de86996f0f795f7", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_59cd8d3aa707294c", "speaker_id": null, "text": "I'm 20, and just got kicked out of my grandmother's house spur of the moment. No idea why, she refuses to tell me, just started throwing things at me and told me \"It's not safe for me to be there.\" I do still have my car, and I have a job so I can afford it. My question is how legal is it to do so? It's a small car, and I'm 6'8, so I doubt I'll get much sleep anyways, but if I do, I wouldn't want to get woken up by police telling me to move, or worse, getting impounded or something."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 3, "excerpt_id": "EXC_1daeebebe862e062", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_e6d1972f8bb65fae", "speaker_id": null, "text": "I've been trying to get in contact with her because I'm scared and worried about her. She isn't answering my phone calls, and will only give a vague text response with an I'll call you later while she is at work. Or HE will text me back and say she is fine and can't talk right now. I spoke to 2 of our mutual friends today and she isn't speaking to them as well. I can feel it in my soul that he is going to seriously hurt her or those babies."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_7f1048200d0ac347", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_eb925de02bd0ed3b", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "Yep, you read the title correctly. I get anxiety from my dog, more specifically leaving my dog alone for extended periods of time. I got him when he was a puppy and at the time I lived at home with four other humans and my parents two dogs. We all worked different schedules so he wasn't left alone very often, and even when we were all gone there were other dogs their with him. A little over a year and a half ago my bf and I moved in together and my dog had some really bad separation anxiety at first.", "candidate_role": "support", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as direct support for the interpretation.", "display_order": 4, "excerpt_id": "EXC_7f1048200d0ac347", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_eb925de02bd0ed3b", "speaker_id": null, "text": "Yep, you read the title correctly. I get anxiety from my dog, more specifically leaving my dog alone for extended periods of time. I got him when he was a puppy and at the time I lived at home with four other humans and my parents two dogs. We all worked different schedules so he wasn't left alone very often, and even when we were all gone there were other dogs their with him. A little over a year and a half ago my bf and I moved in together and my dog had some really bad separation anxiety at first."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_788515e814bd840e", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_786397612eaf4337", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "He used to (while single and during the early phase of our relationship) go out 5 nights a week with friends. Most of these nights would end up between midnight and 2 am. They are harmless. He doesn't drink or do drugs, they don't hang out with girls. It's he and a bunch of old men who like to play pool and poker.", "candidate_role": "counterevidence", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as a boundary case or counterexample.", "display_order": 5, "excerpt_id": "EXC_788515e814bd840e", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_786397612eaf4337", "speaker_id": null, "text": "He used to (while single and during the early phase of our relationship) go out 5 nights a week with friends. Most of these nights would end up between midnight and 2 am. They are harmless. He doesn't drink or do drugs, they don't hang out with girls. It's he and a bunch of old men who like to play pool and poker."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 6, "excerpt_id": "EXC_7bda910988b8adab", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_9c95d0b13815731b", "speaker_id": null, "text": "It has been some time since I posted, but with Fall setting in my anxiety is really getting to me. The cold frightens me, I don't think my partner can survive the weather to come. I used to love Fall, I still do in some ways, but these past couple years really puts into perspective how dangerous it can be. The dread that Winter will be here soon with such instability. But I need the rain; I need the colder temperatures, because I need to have the best mushroom season I have ever had."}], "item_id": "DJI_f6f95b1ef740b922", "item_schema_version": "direction-j-evaluator-item-v1", "output_id": "OUT_f6f95b1ef740b922", "packet_id": "PKT_deee233a3db021cb", "proposed_interpretation": {"boundary_conditions": ["The excerpts describe stress in various contexts, including relationships, work, and personal struggles.", "Some individuals experience stress due to external factors, such as a grandmother's sudden decision to kick them out of the house (EXC_9de86996f0f795f7).", "Others face internal struggles, like anxiety related to leaving their dog alone (EXC_7f1048200d0ac347) or fear of winter weather (EXC_7bda910988b8adab)"], "claim": "People describe and contextualize stress in various ways, including external factors, internal struggles, and personal relationships.", "explanation": "The excerpts suggest that individuals experience stress due to a range of factors, from external events to internal struggles. While some may face challenges related to relationships or work, others may struggle with personal anxieties or fears.", "theme_id": "THM_f6f95b1ef740b922", "theme_name": "Stress Contextualization"}, "research_question": "How do people describe and contextualize experiences of stress?", "source_coverage": {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 3, "candidate_cited_source_count": 3, "coverage_note": "Counts describe only this restricted private packet.", "presented_excerpt_count": 6, "presented_source_count": 6, "sampling_frame_excerpt_count": 6, "sampling_frame_source_count": 6, "source_distribution": [{"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 1, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_59cd8d3aa707294c"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 0, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_71e82d8f0fb03a7f"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 1, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_786397612eaf4337"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 0, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_9c95d0b13815731b"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 0, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_e6d1972f8bb65fae"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 1, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_eb925de02bd0ed3b"}]}}

